  "digitizer_notes": "Re-processed 2026-07-06 after user PASS/FAIL visual audit flagged blue_yellow_forming_layer and green_magenta_forming_layer stopping abruptly (at exposure -2.3 and -1.5 respectively) instead of continuing to converge with red_cyan_forming_layer as the real chart shows. Root cause confirmed directly (raw per-layer pixel inspection): the SEPARATE per-color bitonal image for Green/Blue genuinely has no ink beyond that point in the source PDF -- this is not a tracing bug, Fuji's own file only draws a curve separately where it's visually distinguishable from Red. But the real value IS recoverable there: since only Red's layer is completely drawn, and Green/Blue are printed exactly on top of it once merged, Red's own traced value IS Green/Blue's real value in that stretch. Fix: spliced each of Green/Blue's own real trace with Red's own trace for the region beyond where Green/Blue's separate layer has ink. QA overlay background now composites ALL curve layers (not just the shared frame/gridline layer, which has no curve ink at all in this file format) so the real curve is visible to check the trace against -- previously the background showed only gridlines, making the overlay useless for exactly what it's for. QA overlay: both a combined (all 3 curves) plot and one PNG per curve."
